Stop the double "Saved." confirmation on Settings, standardise it (v0.116)

Settings > Save Settings was showing two save confirmations at once: a
small white "Saved." pill next to the button, and the global green corner
toast (ToastContext) - both fixed to the same bottom-right corner, so they
landed directly on top of each other. Meanwhile most other Save buttons in
the app (Sales Activity order edit, tickets, products, account settings)
only ever showed the green toast, with no pill at all - inconsistent with
Settings and, per feedback, the less preferred of the two.

Fix: a new shared SavedBadge component (frontend/src/components/
SavedBadge.tsx) renders that white pill, and it's now used everywhere a
Save button's page/form stays on screen after saving - Settings, Account
Settings, Product, Ticket, and Sales Activity order edit - with the green
toast call removed from each of those "Saved." confirmations.

The green toast is kept only where it's still the right tool:
- "Order created." (Sales Activity) - creating a new order navigates to
  its real URL, remounting the page before a local pill would ever be
  seen, so the toast (which lives above that remount) is the only thing
  that survives to be shown.
- "Ticket created.", "Deleted.", "DPD shipment booked.", "Label sent to
  printer." - none of these are a "Saved." confirmation sitting next to a
  button that's still on screen.
- Contacts and Companies inline-edit rows - the edit form collapses the
  instant the save succeeds, so there's no button left to anchor a pill
  to; the toast is the only feedback that survives that collapse.
- Goods In - already had its own on-page "Session saved..." banner, so
  the toast there was just removed rather than replaced with anything.

